From: OpenWrt local build <openwrt-local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] backports: retain hex helper declarations on Linux 7.3

Linux 7.3 moved mac_pton and the other hex helpers out of linux/kernel.h
into linux/hex.h. The 7.2 wireless sources still rely on the older kernel
header's declarations. Include the new header in the compatibility wrapper
so all such callers retain their existing declarations.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt local build <openwrt-local@localhost>
---
--- a/backport-include/linux/kernel.h
+++ b/backport-include/linux/kernel.h
@@ -3,6 +3,10 @@
 #include_next <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/version.h>
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(7, 3, 0)
+#include <linux/hex.h>
+#endif
+
 #if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(4,17,0)
 
 /*
